<%# Illustrative split of a $100 rewards-card sale. Interchange and assessments are published network figures; the markup is a placeholder until the Valmar statement is read. %>
<figure class="lms-figure" aria-labelledby="fig-fee-split">
  <figcaption id="fig-fee-split" class="lms-figure-caption">Where the fees on a $100 card sale go (illustration)</figcaption>
  <div class="lms-feebar" role="img" aria-label="Of $100, about $97.65 reaches us; $1.65 goes to the customer's bank as interchange, 14 cents to the card network, and about 56 cents to the processor, gateway and Valmar in this example">
    <span class="lms-feebar-seg lms-feebar-keep" style="width: 87%"><span>We keep ≈ $97.65</span></span>
    <span class="lms-feebar-seg lms-feebar-interchange" style="width: 8%"><span class="sr-only">Interchange</span></span>
    <span class="lms-feebar-seg lms-feebar-assess" style="width: 2%"><span class="sr-only">Assessments</span></span>
    <span class="lms-feebar-seg lms-feebar-markup" style="width: 3%"><span class="sr-only">Markup</span></span>
  </div>
  <ul class="lms-feebar-legend">
    <li><span class="lms-feebar-dot lms-feebar-interchange"></span><strong>$1.65 interchange</strong> → the customer's bank. Set by the network per card type (Visa “Traditional Rewards” card-present rate shown: 1.65% + $0.10).</li>
    <li><span class="lms-feebar-dot lms-feebar-assess"></span><strong>≈ $0.14 assessments</strong> → the card network (≈ 0.14% on Visa and Mastercard credit).</li>
    <li><span class="lms-feebar-dot lms-feebar-markup"></span><strong>≈ $0.56 markup</strong> → processor, gateway and Valmar. The only part that is negotiated. Check our statement for the real figure.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="lms-figure-note">Segments are not to scale. The same $100 on a regulated debit card costs about $0.26 in interchange (0.05% + $0.21) instead of $1.65.</p>
</figure>
